From: nerves_system_fp3 <devs@spin42.com>
Date: Sat, 17 May 2026 09:40:00 +0200
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: fp3p: fix AK7374 VCM I²C address

The DT had the rear-camera VCM at I²C address 0x18, which produced
`ak7375_vcm_resume I2C failure: -6` at every boot — ENXIO from an
unanswered probe. An i2cdetect-style scan of the CCI bus showed the
actuator actually responds at **0x0c** (reg 0x00 returns sensible
position bytes), matching the 7-bit address in the AK73xx datasheet.

The 0x18 in the original node looks like it came from confusing the
8-bit write address (0x18 = 0x0c << 1) with the 7-bit Linux DT form.
Fixing the address lets the upstream ak7375 driver successfully bring
the VCM out of standby and drive the focus position register, which
in turn lets contrast-detect AF in userspace actually move the lens.

Signed-off-by: nerves_system_fp3 <devs@spin42.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm632-fairphone-fp3p.dts | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm632-fairphone-fp3p.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm632-fairphone-fp3p.dts
index aaaaaaaaaaaa..bbbbbbbbbbbb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm632-fairphone-fp3p.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm632-fairphone-fp3p.dts
@@ -658,9 +658,9 @@
 	};

 	/* AK7374 voice coil motor — rear camera autofocus */
-	actuator: camera-lens@18 {
+	actuator: camera-lens@c {
 		compatible = "asahi-kasei,ak7374";
-		reg = <0x18>;
+		reg = <0x0c>;

 		vdd-supply = <&cam_vaf>;
 		vio-supply = <&cam_vio>;
